{"name":"Midnight Cordovan","hex":"#511b18","fetched":"2026-10-24","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"midnight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The middle of the night: the sixth temporal hour, equidistant between sunset and sunrise.","Twelve o'clock at night exactly."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Utterly dark or black."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/midnight"},{"term":"cordovan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Originating in or pertaining to Córdoba."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A kind of leather from Córdoba, originally of tanned goatskin, later of horsehide.","A shoe made from such leather."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cordovan"}],"entries":[{"title":"Midnight","blocks":[{"text":"Midnight is the transition time from one day to the next – the moment when the date changes, on the local official clock time for any particular jurisdiction. By clock time, midnight is the opposite of noon, differing from it by 12 hours."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Tour_de_l%27horloge_de_la_gare_de_Metz_%C3%A0_Minuit_%28juin_2019%29_%28cropped%29.JPG/330px-Tour_de_l%27horloge_de_la_gare_de_Metz_%C3%A0_Minuit_%28juin_2019%29_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight","wikidata":"Q36402"},{"title":"Midnight blue","blocks":[{"text":"Midnight blue is a dark shade of blue named for its resemblance to the apparently blue color of a moonlit night sky around a full moon. Midnight blue is identifiably blue to the eye in sunlight or full-spectrum light, but can appear black under certain more limited spectra sometimes found in artificial lighting. It is similar to navy, which is also a dark blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg/330px-D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight_blue","wikidata":"Q947638"},{"title":"Cordovan (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Cordovan is a rich, dark shade of burgundy with a hint of rose. Cordovan takes its name from the city of Córdoba, Spain, where the production of cordovan leather was first practiced by the Visigoths in the seventh century. The term cordovan has come to describe the color of clothing – leather in particular; in this sense, the use of cordovan overlaps with that of oxblood."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cordovan_(color)","wikidata":"Q5170059"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Tour_de_l%27horloge_de_la_gare_de_Metz_%C3%A0_Minuit_%28juin_2019%29_%28cropped%29.JPG/500px-Tour_de_l%27horloge_de_la_gare_de_Metz_%C3%A0_Minuit_%28juin_2019%29_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Tour_de_l%27horloge_de_la_gare_de_Metz_%C3%A0_Minuit_%28juin_2019%29_%28cropped%29.JPG/1280px-Tour_de_l%27horloge_de_la_gare_de_Metz_%C3%A0_Minuit_%28juin_2019%29_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Tour_de_l%27horloge_de_la_gare_de_Metz_%C3%A0_Minuit_%28juin_2019%29_%28cropped%29.JPG/500px-Tour_de_l%27horloge_de_la_gare_de_Metz_%C3%A0_Minuit_%28juin_2019%29_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Midnight at Metz railway station, in France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATour_de_l'horloge_de_la_gare_de_Metz_%C3%A0_Minuit_(juin_2019)_(cropped).JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Midnight_Mist.jpg/500px-Midnight_Mist.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Midnight_Mist.jpg/500px-Midnight_Mist.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Photograph of the moon taken at midnight","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMidnight_Mist.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg/500px-D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg/1280px-D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg/500px-D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Midnight sky in Düsseldorf, Germany","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AD%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg"}],"sounds":{"midnight":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/36/En-us-midnight.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/36/En-us-midnight.ogg/En-us-midnight.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Ford Madox Brown - The Last of England - Google Art Project","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Ford_Madox_Brown_-_The_Last_of_England_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Ford_Madox_Brown_-_The_Last_of_England_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg","ratio":0.8934045986284792,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ford_Madox_Brown_-_The_Last_of_England_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg","share":0.080625},{"title":"Arthur Brown 2025","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Arthur_Brown_2025.jpg/500px-Arthur_Brown_2025.jpg","ratio":0.6666666666666666,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arthur_Brown_2025.jp